# =============================================================================
# HireSnap - line-ending and binary normalisation.
#
# WHY every file is forced to LF: this stack runs Linux containers from a
# repository routinely checked out on Windows (the reference checkout is at
# R:\HireSnap). git's default core.autocrlf=true rewrites text files to CRLF on
# checkout, and a CRLF shebang is not a subtle bug - the kernel reads the
# interpreter as "/bin/bash\r" and the container dies with
# "bash\r: No such file or directory" before the first line of the script runs.
# The failures are invisible in a diff and only appear inside a container.
# Mirror of R:\GPTHub\.gitattributes:1-6.
# =============================================================================

* text=auto eol=lf

# --- scripts and Dockerfiles: strictly LF, always -------------------------
# These are the files that EXECUTE inside a container. text=auto alone is not
# enough: it lets a file be classified binary (making the rule a no-op) and it
# honours the user's autocrlf for anything it cannot classify.
# Mirror of R:\GPTHub\.gitattributes:8-12.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.bash          text eol=lf
*.template      text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
Makefile        text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf

# --- binaries: never touch ------------------------------------------------
# A CRLF rewrite of a PNG does not corrupt it (git only normalises text), but
# declaring binary stops git from ever attempting a text diff, merge or eol
# conversion on content where that would silently change the bytes:
# certificate/key material in particular must round-trip byte for byte or every
# signature ever issued against it fails to verify.
# Mirror of R:\GPTHub\.gitattributes:14-24.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.webp   binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.pt     binary
*.pth    binary
*.onnx   binary
*.bin    binary
*.npy    binary
*.pem    binary
*.key    binary
*.crt    binary
# Note: `git check-attr` still reports "eol: lf" for these, because the
# catch-all `* text=auto eol=lf` above sets eol on every path. It is inert:
# git applies eol conversion only when text is set, and `binary` (a built-in
# macro for -text -diff -merge) unsets it. Verified: these paths report
# "text: unset / diff: unset / merge: unset". Do not "fix" the apparent
# contradiction by adding an eol rule here - that would be the rule that
# rewrites PEM material.

# --- vendored checkpoints -------------------------------------------------
# backend/cosmos_tokenizer is vendored source (mirror of an upstream package).
# Marking it vendored keeps "git log"/"git diff" from attributing upstream
# history to this repository and keeps the diff reviewable.
backend/cosmos_tokenizer/** linguist-vendored
